 "notes": "Single OCR map sheet; the map face is garbled. Units under an alloformation heading are associated with it from the layout and flagged inferred; symbols printed after descriptions likewise. Garbled symbols not recorded: 'QuHabf' (between beach sand and beach ridge sand), '[ aPtas |' (Ladson barrier deposits), 'OP' (Princess Anne estuarine). Corrected text-layer characters ('|' for 1, 'aFpas', 'Pamiico') are flagged inferred or noted. Bodies of water and disturbed ground not recorded as units. The sheet says its products are provided 'as is' without warranty.\nSUBSURFACE: p. 1 gives the elevation range of each alloformation's seaward and landward margins (Silver Bluff 6-10 ft, Princess Anne 10-18 ft, Pamlico 17-25 ft, Ten Mile Hill 25-35 ft, Ladson 35-57 ft), stored as unit descriptions. Drill holes (e.g. 26-373) are plotted with SCGS log numbers but no depths; logs are on file at SCGS. No cross section or structure-contour map on this sheet. Datum: horizontal 1927 North American Datum, contour interval 2 meters; vertical datum for the elevations not stated.",
